// The ARRANGEMENT — the timeline, and the transport that rolls through it.
//
// A project draws one because it says so here: the timeline is a SURFACE
// (packages/song/docs/surfaces.md), not something the editor hands out for free. Take this
// file away and the song still compiles and still plays — you simply have no lanes on screen.
//
// `split` is what puts it in the layout, sharing the window with the graph underneath, and is
// the only layout a timeline draws in. `view` is the other one: a screen of its own off the
// header, which is where a turntables desk goes.
type("timeline")
layout("split")
